title: event_oldProbe
color: purple
position: 0, 0
---
You notice a wierdly shaped object on your path. As you approach it you notice it is an old probe, probably sent here a century ago. Your sensors detect faint radio signals emitted from it.
-> Avoid the probe
	<<if simple_m_check(55)>>
	Better not to disturb the ghosts of old and their wicked technology.
	<<else>>
	You poor stearing makes you smash directly into the probe.. It shatters into tousands littile pieces. A piece of history is now gone... You ask yourself if you maybe did it on purpose...
	<<if damage_ship(3)>><<endif>>
	<<endif>>
-> Investigate
	<<if simple_m_check(75)>>
	As you carefully maneuver close to the probe, the radio signal grows stronger. As binary beeping fills the cabin, you feel some kind of awe for a by-gone era this probe must have come from. Your Kompat decodes the binary data and it seems that the probe is transmitting telemetry. It's useless to you, but it doesn't feel like it. It's like you received a blessing from the past.
	<<if pass_time(2)>><<endif>>
	<<else>>
	You smash into the probe. It shatters into tousands littile pieces. Maybe you can invastigate a cloud of crumbly, littile metal pieces... better go.
	<<if damage_ship(1)>><<endif>>
	<<endif>>
===
title: event_carelessness
color: purple
position: 0, 0
---
Short routes like these have a tendency to make you careless
-> Trust your instincts
	<<if simple_m_check(20)>>
	No thought given yet you land perfectly. You must truly be a natural pilot or in lady luck's good graces.
	<<else>>
	You crash. Maybe this will serve as motivation to focus in the future.
	<<if damage_ship(5)>><<endif>>
	<<endif>>
-> Focus
	<<if simple_m_check(50)>>
	You land the ship. Lost a bit of time to make sure you do everything up to code but it payed of.
	<<if pass_time(1)>><<endif>>
	<<else>>
	You crash. There is some minor damage but you will be fine. Better focus more next time?
	<<if pass_time(1)>><<endif>>
	<<if damage_ship(1)>><<endif>>
	<<endif>>
-> Extra focus
	<<if simple_m_check(70)>>
	You land the ship. It seems that you only lost time checking every thing trice before the procedure, but you landed safely.
	<<if pass_time(2)>><<endif>>
	<<else>>
	You crash. It seems that borderline paranoia of checking everything thrice may have caused you to perform too slowly. Better chill next time?
	<<if pass_time(2)>><<endif>>
	<<if damage_ship(2)>><<endif>>
	<<endif>>
===
